From 3f6a3411616cc23937e69a584bb1f6712ba57d17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 16:37:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08536/11362] [outer-loop] correct commit f75998dbcd: remove
 accidentally-included conductor in-flight work

The previous commit (f75998dbcd, REQ-ARC-WMTE-6227) staged
arc_executable_world_model.py with `git add <path>`, which picked up the
WHOLE working-tree diff for that file -- not just this session's own edit.
The conductor's own separate, uncommitted REQ-ARC-WMTE-6213 work
(_object_delta_perception_block and its one-line call site in
induce_prompt) was mixed into that commit as a result, breaking this
session's own established discipline (documented repeatedly in earlier
commit messages today) of verifying `git diff -U0 | grep '^@@'` shows only
this session's own hunks before staging a file the conductor is also
actively editing.

This commit removes exactly those two hunks (verified via a hunk-level
diff reconstruction: this session's hunks + the conductor's hunks applied
together to the pre-f75998dbcd base reproduce f75998dbcd's committed
content byte-for-byte, so this correction removes precisely and only the
conductor's contribution). REQ-ARC-WMTE-6227's own fix
(_INDUCE_WORST_CASE_PROMPT_TOKENS + the _default_induce_n_ctx docstring
correction) is untouched. The conductor's work is not lost -- it is
restored as an uncommitted working-tree diff right after this commit,
exactly as it stood before the mistake, so the conductor can commit it
normally under its own message when it resumes.

No functional regression either way: _object_delta_perception_block is
gated behind CARNOT_ARC_OBJECT_DELTA_PERCEPTION (default off) and the
whole call site degrades to a no-op via try/except if the module is
absent, so its presence or absence in this commit was never a behavior
change for the shipped default -- this is a provenance/attribution
correction, not a functional fix.

Also acknowledges 7 results/ artifacts flagged stale by the artifact-
freshness-lint, since this correction changes the file's hash again; the
reachability argument is unchanged from the immediately-prior
acknowledgement pass on these same 7 artifacts for REQ-ARC-WMTE-6227.

